{"kind":"assert","text":"Still open, and now proved by mutation rather than argued. Measured against main at 97ab60c3.\n\nThe condition asks for a stubbed globalThis.localStorage so the personal-work storage wiring is exercised, and then for confirmation that four named reversions fail. Main does have a localStorage stub, added by 04ca956a, but it is aimed somewhere else: it exercises the storage helpers directly — savePersonalWorkMemory, loadPersonalWorkMemory, followWorkTopic, viewWorkTopic — and never goes through the component. The gap this request names is the component-to-storage wiring, and initialPersonalMemory is still a prop on WorkDrawer and still supplies memory directly at ui/test/components.test.mjs:303, which is the affordance the review objected to.\n\nSo I tested the first of the four reversions instead of reasoning about it. In a detached worktree at main I replaced the mount-load effect in ui/src/components/WorkDrawer.tsx — the useEffect that calls loadPersonalWorkMemory and sets personal state — with an empty body, and ran the UI suite. It passed: 72 tests, zero failures. Removing the component's load-on-mount entirely breaks no test.\n\nThat is the condition failing on its own terms. The request asks that this reversion fail; it passes. I checked one of the four named reversions, not all four, and I am saying so rather than implying a complete sweep; but a single surviving mutation is enough to show the wiring is uncovered, and it is the first one the request lists.\n\nThe baseline passed before the mutation and the worktree is removed, so nothing here changed main or any branch.\n\nWorth separating two things for whoever takes this, because they read alike on a green suite. Personal-work storage is well covered as a module: isolation by room and exact actor, rejection of malformed stored fields, follow and view semantics. What is uncovered is that the component actually calls it. A reader seeing those storage tests pass would reasonably conclude the feature is tested, which is the precise shape of the affordance the original review objected to."}